=================================================================
Step 5: Family is Legendre family at lambda = -q^2
=================================================================

E_PCP(q) = Legendre family E_lambda with lambda = -q^2.

j(E_PCP(q)) = 256 (1 + q^2 + q^4)^3 / (q^4 (1+q^2)^2)

Verify with formal computation:

j(q) = (256*q^12 + 768*q^10 + 1536*q^8 + 1792*q^6 + 1536*q^4 + 768*q^2 + 256)/(q^8 + 2*q^6 + q^4)

--- Family modular structure ---

The Legendre family Y^2 = X(X-1)(X-lambda) over lambda-line is the
universal elliptic curve over Y(2) = X(2) - {cusps}.

Pythagorean parametrization: q = (m^2-n^2)/(2mn) traces a curve
C_{Pyth}: lambda = -q^2 in the lambda-line.

C_{Pyth} as a subvariety:
  lambda + q^2 = 0  with q = (m^2-n^2)/(2mn)
  Equivalently: lambda = -((m^2-n^2)/(2mn))^2
  Set s = m/n: lambda = -(s^2-1)^2/(4s^2)^2 * (2n^2)^2/(2n^2)^2
                       = -(s^2-1)^2/(4s)^2 ... function of s only.

So C_{Pyth} = image of P^1_s under s -> -((s-1/s)/2)^2 = -((s^2-1)/(2s))^2

--- Degree of parametrization s -> lambda(s) = -((s^2-1)/(2s))^2 ---

Critical points of lambda(s): s = +-1, 1 +- sqrt(2)
Critical values lambda: 0, 0, -((1+sqrt2)^2-1)^2/(4(1+sqrt2)^2)

--- Family L-function (in the moment / averaging sense) ---

L(s, family) := lim_{X -> inf} (1/N(X)) sum_{(m,n) : 2mn <= X}
                   L(s, E_PCP(q(m,n)))

By Sarnak-Shin-Templier / Bhargava-Shankar, family Selmer rank
controls the AVERAGE rank.  For the Pythagorean family above:

