--- Interpretation ---

If L(1, E_{m,n}) != 0, then by Kolyvagin + modularity: rank(E_{m,n}) = 0.
If L(1, E_{m,n}) == 0, then rank >= 1 (and = ord_{s=1} L(s) by BSD).

In our data, L(1) for the Pythagorean family appears to be NONZERO
for all sampled (m,n). This (if it holds uniformly) is exactly the
rank-jump exclusion we need.
